6  23 on your wednesday morning hey we're  checking in on the status  of those hov lanes well the bottom line  for now  is that hov lanes can only legally be  driven if there are two or more people  in a vehicle  any time of the day or night there are a  couple of exceptions motorcycles rtc  buses and emergency vehicles well the  nevada department of transportation says  it  may take a look at modifying the 24 7  status of those lanes but  don't expect anything to change anytime  soon ndot's tony ilya tells me  we are tentatively looking to commission  an 18-month study  to determine the high peak use hours of  hov lanes in clark county  he says the results could provide  guidance toward future hov  operational decisions but even that  study's not a done deal tony adds a  contract won't come before the state  transportation board until may  or possibly june so the bottom line not  much changing right now we'll keep you  posted buckle up drive carefully please  put down that phone  if there's something driving you crazy  email me traffic eight at  eightnewsnow.com

